  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving access to family planning for people with disabilities in northern Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to promote access to inclusive family planning for people with disabilities in Northern Nigeria. The project will last for three years (starting in January 2022) and will aim to achieve three key outcomes:1. People with disabilities having increased knowledge of, intention to use, and perceived support from others to access, available family planning services.2. Service providers delivering inclusive, accessible healthcare services and information to people with disabilities.3. OPDs meaningfully engaging in policy and decision-making processes and advocating for disability inclusion in the health sector through different structures.Ultimately, through the achievement of these outcomes, the project aims to contribute to the reduction of unmet need for family planning and increased access to and use of available modern contraceptive methods by people with disabilities in the target project areas.</narrative>
  </description>
